@ version:  1.0
@ creator:  q-ai.nl
@ summary:  Rotating async CSRF protection for Phlo requests
@ advice:   The token rotates: every verified request answers with a new one, so a stolen token is worth one request at most. That only works if the page keeps the answer, which the frontend does on its own; a hand-written fetch has to send the current token as X-CSRF-Token and store the new one. It protects a session, so it says nothing about an API authenticated with a bearer token.
@ package:  security
@ frontend: true
@ backend:  true
@ requires: @session token payload
@ provides: app.mod.csrf
@ tags:     csrf security async forms

view: <meta name=csrf content="$this->token">
prop token:string => %session->csrf ??= token(32)
method verify:bool => hash_equals($this->token, (string)($_SERVER['HTTP_X_CSRF_TOKEN'] ?? void))
method update:array => arr(csrf: $this->token = %session->csrf = token(32))

<script>
app.mod.csrf = value => obj('meta[name="csrf"]').content = value
</script>
